RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) – Complete Concept
1. 🌟 Real-Life Scenario
Socho tumne ek AI Tool / Chatbot banaya hai jo sirf tumhari university ki website ke baare mein information provide kare.

Tum chahte ho ke:
- User university ke admission ke baare mein pooche to AI admission ki information de.
- User university ki fee ke baare mein pooche to AI fee ki information de.
- Lekin agar user cricket, politics ya kisi doosre topic ke baare mein pooche to AI uska jawab na de.
Ab problem ye hai ke normal AI ke paas bohat saari general information hoti hai. Woh university ke topic se bahar bhi jawab de sakta hai.

Solution: RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation)

RAG implement karne se AI pehle apne specific knowledge database se relevant information retrieve karta hai, phir us information ki help se answer generate karta hai.
2. ❓ What is RAG & Why Do We Need It?
RAG stands for Retrieval-Augmented Generation.

RAG is an AI technique that connects an AI model with an external knowledge source so it can retrieve relevant information and generate answers based on that information.

RAG ke 3 main steps hain:
1. Retrieval (Information Search)
- Retrieval ka matlab hai information ko search karna aur retrieve karna.
- Jab user koi question poochta hai, AI relevant information ko Vector Database se search karta hai.
- Sirf question se related information retrieve ki jati hai.
Example: User asks: "What is the admission fee?"

Retrieval admission fee se related information search karega.
2. Augmentation (Adding Information)
- Augmentation ka matlab hai retrieved information ko AI ke prompt mein add karna.
- AI ko user ke question ke saath relevant context bhi provide kiya jata hai.
- Is se AI ko accurate answer dene mein help milti hai.
Example: Retrieved information: "Admission fee is Rs. 20,000."

Ab ye information AI ko user ke question ke saath di jayegi.
3. Generation (Answer Creation)
- Generation ka matlab hai answer generate karna.
- AI retrieved information aur user ke question ko understand karke final answer generate karta hai.
Example: "The university admission fee is Rs. 20,000."
